WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.740
Already getting pumped for the arrival of
Vin Diesel's new cinematic universe?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.460
We've gone and rounded up the best rumors
and spoilers the internet has to offer.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.720
These are just some of the leaked details
surrounding the Bloodshot movie.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.280
According to Geeks WorldWide, the new Bloodshot
is going to be something of a take on the

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.340
classic revenge tale.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.149
Vin Diesel plays Ray Garrison, a Marine who,
after he and his wife are murdered, is resurrected

00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:22.260
as a super-soldier.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.099
When Garrison's erased memories return, he
sets out to exact revenge on the man responsible

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.840
for his and his wife's deaths.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:33.560
Bloodshot is based on a comic book from publisher
Valiant Comics, which may explain why at first

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.340
glance the character seems reminiscent of
other comic heroes who have been adapted to

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.880
the big screen, such as Deadpool, Winter Soldier,
and Wolverine.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.540
But former editor-in-chief of Valiant and
co-creator of the character Bob Layton assured

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.400
Deadline in 2018 that this is a unique project.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.220
He insisted that he and Bloodshot writer Kevin
VanHook:

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.280
"...worked very, very hard to give Bloodshot
a voice that was very different from those

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.320
other characters."

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.070
Layton also said Bloodshot's filmmakers have
approached the film with the understanding

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.610
that audiences know comic films.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:02.340
He explained,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.880
"The filmmakers are embracing the current
movie-going audience's knowledge of comic

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.200
book storytelling and have produced something
very fresh and subversive to the genre."

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:16.260
At the beginning of 2018, DMG Entertainment,
the $6 billion media company which co-produced

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:21.100
2012's Looper and 2013's Iron Man 3, took
full control of Valiant Entertainment.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.219
DMG founder Dan Mintz announced:

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.640
"Our priority is to build upon Valiant's vast
universe of characters from a filmmaker's

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.200
perspective.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.620
I'm excited to immerse Valiant's fans well
beyond the stories we tell cinematically,

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.320
from publishing to gaming to theme parks and
beyond."

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:40.300
DMG and Valiant originally set up a partnership
deal in 2015, which included plans for both

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.500
film and television.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.430
So it isn't surprising that Bloodshot is tabbed
as only the beginning of a future franchise

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.200
for the company.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:51.420
Deadline reported that DMG, Valiant, and Sony
had made plans for a five-film series that

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.079
would include Valiant's Bloodshot and Harbinger,
as well as a shared crossover film called

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.280
Harbinger Wars.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:01.539
In a 2017 interview with Den of Geek, newly
tapped Bloodshot screenwriter Eric Heisserer

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:05.479
spoke on the importance of not relying on
related films or sequels when approaching

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.480
a franchise film.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.360
Heisserer, who's also been hired to write
the Harbinger script, said he wanted to focus

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.640
on the films as though they were self-contained
stories.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.400
He dished:

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.820
"My goal was to make a great Harbinger script
and a great Bloodshot script, and if audiences

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.620
love those stories, and we were honored enough
to come back and revisit those characters,

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.120
great."

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.300
In his interview with Deadline, Bob Layton
expanded on the idea that Bloodshot wouldn't

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.620
just be another comic franchise film, saying,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.540
"They're really focusing on Vin's character
and it really seems to be a more character-driven

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.220
movie, rather than just a lot of big explosions…"

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:39.360
Explaining how comics films tend to rely too
heavily on third act fight scenes, Layton

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.470
said the key to a good superhero film is to
keep the focus on the character, as opposed

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.100
to making it a, quote, "giant roller coaster
ride."

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.720
In July 2018, sources told Key Collector Comics
that two villains would appear in Bloodshot.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:56.760
The first to be identified was the computer-obsessed
Ax, who made his debut in Harbinger #3.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.590
His thirst for technology would eventually
lead him to seek out Bloodshot in order to

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.260
steal his nanite-enhanced blood.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.200
The Wrap reported that Fantastic Four's Toby
Kebbell would be playing the character.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.980
At the same time, The Wrap confirmed that
Game of Thrones actor Johannes Haukur Johannesson

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:14.420
had been added to the cast as a second villain,
although who exactly he would be playing was

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.380
still unknown.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.920
According to IMDb, however, Johannesson is
listed as portraying a character named Nick

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.520
Baris.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.000
Since it's been established that the film's
premise will differ from the comics, it's

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.480
still hard to say who exactly Nick Baris is
in the Bloodshot universe.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.000
When The Wrap first reported that Vin Diesel
was in talks to star in Bloodshot in January

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.380
2018, the film had been described as an

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.420
"R-rated take on the comic adaptation that
will be tonally and aesthetically influenced

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:43.460
by high-concept, sci-fi blockbusters of the
late '80s including Robocop, Terminator, and

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:44.140
Total Recall."

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.930
That R rating seemed to mean that Bloodshot
would be following in the footsteps of other

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.000
recent, non-traditional comic films like Logan
and Deadpool.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.780
"That does it!

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:55.880
Oh!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.540
Canada, that's not good."

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.660
More recently, however, it's looked as though
Bloodshot could potentially be going for a

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.320
PG-13 rating.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.320
As noted by DiscussingFilm, which shared the
film's first full synopsis in March 2019,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:15.000
a PG-13 rating would allow Sony to reach a
wider audience, as well as a "consistent wider

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.840
market" for the studio's planned Valiant Cinematic
Universe.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.720
Since the character is known for its "hard
R" persona, the decision to give the movie

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.860
a more family-friendly edge may wind up backfiring
for Sony.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.199
For fans familiar with the Bloodshot comic
series, Ray Garrison's look is pretty unmistakable;

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.259
pale skin, black hair, red eyes.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.040
He also has a penchant for running around
without a shirt on.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.690
So when Vin Diesel posted the first image
from the film to his Instagram account in

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.240
January 2019, it wasn't exactly what fans
were expecting.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.680
The image, which shows a pretty regular-looking
Diesel in a camouflage jacket, aviator shades,

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.419
and without any hair, is a far cry from the
Bloodshot of the comics.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.120
Diesel captioned the pic:

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.789
"Ray Garrison is a central character in the
Valiant Comic Universe…And for me personally,

00:04:55.789 --> 00:04:58.750
one of the [most] complex characters I have
been fortunate enough to play.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.980
Hope to make you proud…#BLOODSHOT"

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.420
Of course, it's entirely possible that this
first image is of Ray before his forced nanite

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:09.140
procedure, and that in the coming months we'll
be able to see more of the character from

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:09.860
Valiant's pages.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.380
But it's certainly a start.

